They couldn't engineer a better solution

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.730
but you know what, fine.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.340
Oh, fatal flaw, we got the top down camera

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.643
and I have no way of showing
it to the top down, wait.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.472
A solution.

00:01:55.472 --> 00:01:57.090
(laughing)

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.540
Now the performance
embargo hasn't lifted yet

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.590
but we can talk about all
the detailed specs and Intel

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.803
has released enough performance
information about this GPU

00:02:07.803 --> 00:02:11.190
that we can make some
pretty educated guesses.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.456
First the basics though,
the ARC lineup is divided

00:02:13.456 --> 00:02:17.160
up into three, five, and
seven series products

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.130
just like you would see
on their desktop CPU's.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.190
So this being an A770 makes it

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.680
the top performer of their top series.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.820
It uses their DG2-512 processor,
clocked at 2.1 gigahertz.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.817
That means it has 32 of their Xe cores

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:34.230
and 32 ray-tracing units.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:38.220
It's equipped with eight or
16 gigabytes of video memory.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.050
That's what makes this
the limited edition.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.200
It has 16 gigs of memory
and that's connected via

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.200
a 256 bit bus and it's rated
to draw 225 watts of power.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:54.170
Which is our first red
flag because Intel says

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.240
that this card is designed
to compete against

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.750
NVIDIA's RTX 3060 and
AMD's Radeon RX 6650 XT,

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.150
both of which draw in the
neighborhood of 160 to 170 watts.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Also, neither of which
use a 256 bit memory bus.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.070
That means that, especially
once we dig in a little deeper,

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:20.280
and find the transistor
count of this card that Intel

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.270
was hoping for better
performance out of this GPU.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:29.270
More along the lines of a
3070 or a 6700 class card.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.524
Making matters more complicated for Intel,

00:03:31.524 --> 00:03:35.723
NVIDIA has already announced
their RTX 40 Series of cards.

00:03:35.723 --> 00:03:39.707
However, NVIDIA's pricing
is so far out to lunch

00:03:39.707 --> 00:03:42.540
that if, at the price Intel has announced,

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.870
which is 330 dollars for
this card, they do manage

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.860
to be competitive with a 3060, 3060 Ti.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.780
And if the overclocking head room

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.848
is anywhere near what
they've talked about,

00:03:53.848 --> 00:03:58.080
ARC could actually end up
being pretty competitive.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.730
I guess we should take a
closer look at the card.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.339
Man, did they ever nail the aesthetics.

00:04:01.339 --> 00:04:04.663
You've got a diffused RGB strip down here.

00:04:04.663 --> 00:04:07.860
Diffused RGB lighting
around both of the fans.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.880
Man, in real life, once
it's lit, it looks amazing.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.560
Oh, do you have a test
bench for me right there?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.450
Bella Mans has got a test bench for me.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:16.283
Hey, thank you.

